[{"finding":"When a value crosses a process/language boundary to multiple consumers, fix moves to the consumers, never to the emitter — the emitter's spelling is treated as fixed even when it predates the consumers","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/observations/run-audit.ts:40"],"released":false},{"finding":"A cross-boundary consistency test derives its expected value by parsing the authoritative source's own literal, rather than trusting a second constant hand-copied beside it","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/capture/dispatch-action.test.ts:29"],"released":false},{"finding":"When historical records violate a newly-introduced invariant and cannot be repaired, the entries that violate it are dropped with a logged count, and the pipeline proceeds on the resulting wider approximation rather than failing the run","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/observations/run-audit.ts:130"],"released":false},{"finding":"A trigger gate is chosen from the event field that identifies who performed the act (sender/author_association) rather than a label or state that anyone can cause to exist.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".github/workflows/shape.yml:44"],"released":false},{"finding":"When repairing a stale citation, the session sometimes resolved the surrounding claim's substance (introducing a new \"decided\" state, e.g. branch protection declined) rather than only replacing the dead pointer, without flagging that as a separate judgement call.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".claude/hooks/gauntlet-hook.mjs:5"],"released":false},{"finding":"When removing a locally-mirrored artifact whose canonical copy lives at an external URL, delete the local citation path entirely rather than keeping it alongside the URL","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":["GOAL.md:227"],"released":false},{"finding":"Test doubles for two dependencies whose relative order matters are logged into one shared call-sequence array rather than separate counters, so ordering assertions read off a single list.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/watchdog/back-stamp.test.ts:233"],"released":false},{"finding":"Assertions over a corpus that can grow over time are expressed as properties (plus their logical converse) instead of a pinned literal count, so the test doesn't go red merely because the corpus grew.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/watchdog/missing-trailer.test.ts:96"],"released":false},{"finding":"A non-gate helper degrades by skipping work it can't complete rather than failing outright, reserving fail-closed behavior for the actual gate that will catch the same problem downstream.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":["bin/new-adr:101"],"released":false},{"finding":"A file meant partly for model injection separates human-facing explanatory prose from the injected content behind a delimiter, and the accessor throws rather than silently returning an empty or over-inclusive result if the split fails","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/to-tickets/to-tickets.ts:286"],"released":false},{"finding":"A small error-preserving-and-rethrow wrapper is duplicated at a second failure site instead of generalized into one shared helper, despite the new function's own comment describing it as making \"the same bargain\" as the existing one","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/to-tickets/to-tickets.ts:393"],"released":false},{"finding":"A test's fixture parser splits on a maximally permissive delimiter and asserts shape explicitly afterward, rather than matching a pattern that could silently skip a malformed entry","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/to-tickets/vocabulary.test.ts:21"],"released":false},{"finding":"Validate every item in a batch before performing any side effect on any of them, so a single invalid item leaves zero effects rather than a partial write.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/acceptance/acceptance.ts:138"],"released":false},{"finding":"When two options represent mutually exclusive semantics, refuse the call at the very top of the function before any other work runs, rather than picking a resolution order between them.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/stage.ts:285"],"released":false},{"finding":"A gate that can silently drop a true positive must be built from deterministic lookups against already-produced artifacts rather than a model's judgement, because a wrong drop is invisible downstream.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/review/structural-refusal.ts:80"],"released":false},{"finding":"A `gh`-workflow-YAML test reads and parses the workflow file directly (`readFileSync` + `yaml.parse`) instead of using the shared `readWorkflow` helper this diff introduces for exactly that purpose, unlike every sibling workflow test in the same diff.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/review/review.test.ts:296"],"released":false},{"finding":"Parsing the issue number back out of `gh issue create`'s stdout (a `/\\/issues\\/(\\d+)\\s*$/`-style regex plus a \"could not parse an issue number\" throw) is reimplemented verbatim per module instead of being factored into one shared helper.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/review/publish-findings.ts:16"],"released":false},{"finding":"Cross-lane dispatch event-type constants get exactly one declaration, and are guarded by a test that reads the wire name out of every receiving workflow's `if:` and checks it against that single constant, rather than each side testing its own imported copy.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/immutable-set.test.ts:135"],"released":false},{"finding":"A `repository_dispatch` trigger branch carries no separate sender/actor authorization check (no `sender.login` or `author_association` gate), because sending the dispatch itself already required write access, so the send is treated as the authorization.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/spec-workflow.test.ts:75"],"released":false},{"finding":"A dispatch payload field's encoding (comma-joined string vs. repeated `key[]=` array) is chosen based on how the specific downstream job parses it — comma-joined for a shell string-compare job, a real repeated array for a job that reads it as JSON.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/implement/implement.ts:300"],"released":false},{"finding":"An issue's label is applied on the same `gh issue create` call that files it, never as a follow-up `issue edit`, so the issue is never observable in an unlabeled state that other automation could read as an ordinary issue.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/spec/publish.ts:139"],"released":false},{"finding":"A cross-call ordering guarantee is tested by comparing call indices (`findIndex`/`toBeGreaterThan`) to prove one action happened strictly after another, rather than asserting only that both calls occurred.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shape/accept.test.ts:291"],"released":false},{"finding":"An exemption from an automated reachability/dead-code gate must carry an inline prose reason at the exemption site itself, never a silent name in an ignore list","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/check-contract.ts:57",".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/check-contract.ts:93","knip.config.ts:79"],"released":true},{"finding":"A baseline that grandfathers existing debt into a new gate must only ratchet down and gate solely on new additions, never re-grow or serve as a permanent allowlist","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/wiring-baseline.json:3","docs/agents/clone-gate.md:46"],"released":true},{"finding":"A check-command allowlist keyed to specific remote-reading commands (gh api/issue/pr/run, curl, wget), not a broader \"reaches outside the repository\" heuristic, because a deliberately-outside-repo but locally-readable path must still pass","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/render-body.ts:33"],"released":false},{"finding":"When a test double must echo back untrusted string content that may contain shell metacharacters, write it to a file the stub reads back rather than interpolating it into the stub script's own source","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/render-body.test.ts:76"],"released":false},{"finding":"Context a model needs for correctness is inlined directly into its prompt rather than granted through a tool or allow-list, so its reach is a fact about what was built rather than an instruction it must choose to honor.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/acceptance/acceptance.ts:95"],"released":false},{"finding":"Content rendered into a prompt for a model is left uncapped rather than truncated, since a partial view recreates the same guessing problem the full view was added to remove.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/acceptance/acceptance.ts:101"],"released":false},{"finding":"Structurally distinct absent-states (a claimed file not yet created vs. a ticket that claims no files at all) are given separate, explicit sentinel messages rather than collapsed into one empty or undefined representation.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/acceptance/acceptance.ts:80"],"released":false},{"finding":"A body-section parser is relocated to the shared module that owns the data shape it reads, once a second caller needs the same reading, rather than staying in the file of whichever caller wrote it first.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/ticket-shape.ts:176"],"released":false},{"finding":"A structural text matcher built to read a config/workflow file strips comments before matching, because prose explaining a decision can itself contain text indistinguishable from a real match.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":["tests/acceptance/workflow-shape.fixture.ts:94"],"released":false},{"finding":"A counter that recomputes its entire result set from scratch every run is entitled to close its own standing issue when the count reaches zero, but a counter that only sees a partial slice of state per run must not, since it lacks the full picture to justify closing.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/dispatch/reconcile.ts:341"],"released":false},{"finding":"A failure in a side-effecting close/retire call is caught, logged, and dropped rather than surfaced as a run failure, because the operation is idempotent and the next scheduled run will naturally retry it.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/dispatch/reconcile.ts:354"],"released":false},{"finding":"When an action posts a record that justifies a subsequent state-changing call to an external system, the record-writing call must be ordered before the state-changing call, so a downstream reader of history never observes the change without its justification already present.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/dispatch/reconcile.ts:351"],"released":false},{"finding":"A CI checkout must use fetch-depth: 0 whenever the job runs a test suite that may assert facts about git history rather than the working tree, since shallow clones make history-dependent checks fail on venue artefacts rather than real facts","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".github/workflows/verify.yml:112"],"released":false},{"finding":"Machine-written trailers/markers must be stripped from content before it's shown to a model and deterministically re-appended after the model's output is written back, rather than trusting the model to preserve them verbatim","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/spec/publish.ts:131"],"released":false},{"finding":"A scripted test fake with an ordered list of per-call responses should throw once it runs out of responses rather than silently repeating the last one","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/stage.fake.ts:37"],"released":false},{"finding":"When new work must happen between a decision and its effects, split a combined decide-and-apply function into a pure counting/deciding half and a single shared applying half, rather than duplicating the apply logic per caller","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/spec/spec.ts:323"],"released":false},{"finding":"A stage that revises output already validated by an earlier decision should not have that decision re-checked against its output, since there is no remaining channel to resolve a fresh objection","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/spec/spec.ts:416"],"released":false},{"finding":"When a stage's structured output is naturally a single scalar value, wrap it with a scalar-rooted output schema instead of modeling it as a synthetic single-field object type","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/spec/reconcile.ts:56"],"released":false},{"finding":"An ADR superseded by a later one gets a \"Status: superseded by ADR-NNNN\" line added near its top.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":["docs/adr/0039-the-governor-does-not-ship-concurrency-is-bounded-by-ready-d.md:5"],"released":false},{"finding":"A wait loop that polls an external verdict bounds itself by a fixed attempt count rather than elapsed wall-clock time, so a test can drive it by counting reads instead of advancing a clock.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/integrate/integrate.ts:208"],"released":false},{"finding":"Subprocess-spawning logic reused by more than one lane is extracted into shared/ rather than one lane importing another lane's module at runtime.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/close-ticket.ts:13"],"released":false},{"finding":"A reader's dependency on a specific field existing in an API response is proven against a payload recorded from the live API, not only against a hand-written fake.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/dispatch/closing-prs.fixtures/issue-237-closed-by.json:1"],"released":false},{"finding":"Exit code 2 from a check is read as \"could not run\" only for checks that explicitly opt into that convention, never applied globally, since third-party tools can use exit 2 for a genuine finding.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":["bin/gauntlet:323"],"released":false},{"finding":"A repair step outside a run's primary claim (e.g. regenerating a derived artifact) never fails the run when it errors; the failure is logged and left for a downstream gate to catch by name.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/implement/regenerate-artifacts.ts:72"],"released":false},{"finding":"Fake test IDs for two related-but-distinct entities (e.g. an issue and its closing PR) are deliberately given different numbering schemes so a reader that confuses the two fails the test rather than passing by coincidence.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/dispatch/reconcile.test.ts:54"],"released":false},{"finding":"A caught exception is treated as the specific case it's meant to handle only after positively confirming that case via authoritative post-failure state, and re-thrown unchanged when that confirmation fails","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/integrate/integrate.ts:387"],"released":false},{"finding":"State that a subsequent cleanup or abort operation will destroy is read out before that operation runs","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/integrate/integrate.ts:391"],"released":false},{"finding":"An expensive or irreversible operation's precondition is checked and the call skipped with an explicit no-op message when the precondition doesn't hold, rather than invoking it speculatively","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/fixer/fixer.ts:323"],"released":false},{"finding":"A non-merge outcome only reddens the automation run when the outcome reflects a problem with the diff under test, not merely because nothing was merged","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/integrate/integrate.ts:622"],"released":false},{"finding":"When one file's output format is parsed by another, a test reads both files' sources and asserts the parser's pattern matches the exact string the producer emits, so a rewording in either fails a test instead of breaking silently at runtime","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/fixer/fixer.test.ts:278"],"released":false},{"finding":"A status/label constant with meaning shared across independently-triggered lanes is defined once and imported, never re-declared as a duplicate string literal","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/integrate/integrate.ts:5"],"released":false},{"finding":"Cheap regex prefilter selects candidate lines before a precise structured parse decides the actual verdict, preserving both performance and correctness","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".claude/hooks/_hook.py:399"],"released":false},{"finding":"A hook's per-subprocess deadlines are treated as a shared wall-clock budget that must stay under the harness's registered timeout, with a test asserting the sum against that registered value rather than just documenting it","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".claude/hooks/close-gate.py:79"],"released":false},{"finding":"When a signal is unknowable, the code defaults to whichever answer is safe for that specific gate's failure direction, not a universal fail-open/fail-closed default","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".claude/hooks/_hook.py:453"],"released":false},{"finding":"A lane that performs a write (even without spending a model) must set cancel-in-progress: false, since a cancelled write can leave partial/torn state behind — not just model-spending lanes","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".github/workflows/release-on-prd-close.yml:39"],"released":false},{"finding":"A concurrency group's key must scope to the specific subject a run acts on (e.g. per-PRD, per-issue), never a fixed/shared key, so unrelated subjects don't serialize behind each other","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".github/workflows/to-tickets.yml:63"],"released":false},{"finding":"A \"Cite, don't restate\" trim names a plain code comment (not a helper docstring or an ADR) as the rationale's home","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".github/workflows/verify.yml:116",".Workflow/agent-workflows/fixer/fixer.test.ts:210",".Workflow/agent-workflows/fixer/fixer.test.ts:264"],"released":true},{"finding":"Escalation to the owner goes on the ticket (issue), never the pull request, so the tracker is the single place an agent checks for stalled work","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/needs-human.ts:29"],"released":false},{"finding":"A stopped/failed lane always pairs a machine-readable label with a human-readable comment explaining what was tried — never one without the other","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/fixer/fixer.ts:171"],"released":false},{"finding":"A push/commit made by a lane that may run after another lane already rewrote the branch's history uses `--force-with-lease`, never a plain `push`","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/fixer/fixer.ts:157"],"released":false},{"finding":"A lane that repairs or rebuilds a branch re-checks out and rebases onto trunk immediately before doing lane-specific work, so the code that runs is trunk's rather than whatever the branch originally forked from","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".github/workflows/fixer.yml:249"],"released":false},{"finding":"A dispatch/event handler reads state (e.g. ticket/PR status) before spending any model or expensive work, and refuses cheaply rather than let the expensive stage discover staleness after the fact","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/implement/implement.ts:598"],"released":false},{"finding":"Idempotency/attempt-tracking for an unattended retry loop is derived from durable, externally-inspectable state (commit messages, marker comments) rather than an in-memory or file-based counter, so 