99"],"released":false},{"finding":"A baseline entry whose stored fragment fails to re-hash to its own recorded hash is treated as a gate failure (exit code reserved for \"could not run\") rather than as an ordinary finding, distinguishing data-integrity corruption from legitimate content drift.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/clone-gate.ts:337"],"released":false},{"finding":"Recorded line-number metadata on a baseline entry is deliberately left stale rather than refreshed on every write, trading display accuracy for diff stability against unrelated line-shifting edits.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/clone-gate.ts:542"],"released":false},{"finding":"A one-time schema migration (backfilling a new optional field onto existing records) is folded into the routine maintenance operation rather than implemented as a separate one-off migration step.","lens":"PROPOSED","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/clone-gate.ts:672"],"released":false},{"finding":"**Cite, don't restate** — \"the why behind a shared helper lives once, in the helper's docstring (or the ADR)... Red flag: a comment outside the helper's home that explains what the helper used to do, what the two copies used to disagree on, or why sharing fixed it.\" This comment restates the full `#274`/`fakeGh` example and mechanism already given in `recut()`'s docstring in `clone-gate.ts` almost verbatim, rather than citing `#282`/ADR-0116 and the function name.","lens":"VIOLATION","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/clone-gate.test.ts:193"],"released":true},{"finding":"**Cite, don't restate** — same red flag. This comment re-explains \"the other way a fingerprint moves,\" restating the extent-growth bullet already given in `recut()`'s docstring, instead of citing it.","lens":"VIOLATION","sites":[".Workflow/agent-workflows/shared/clone-gate.test.ts:217"],"released":true},{"finding":"**Cite, don't restate** — same red flag. This comment restates the 